WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.300
Today, we’re getting scary. Scientifically&nbsp;
scary. When a fear becomes so severe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.280
it might get in the way of you living your&nbsp;
normal life, it becomes known as a phobia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.200
We’d wager to say that almost everyone watching&nbsp;
this video suffers from at least one of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.020
and given we’ll be covering a staggering 28&nbsp;
phobias today, there’s a good chance that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:28.920
statistically, one of them is yours. But&nbsp;
we’re SCP Explained, not Phobias Explained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.320
so naturally, we’re going to be putting our&nbsp;
own spin on the concept of debilitating terror.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.140
At the time of this video’s&nbsp;
recording, there are well over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:43.080
6000 anomalies documented by the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation. Some are cute and adorable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:51.300
Some are funny. Some are badass. But most of them&nbsp;
are pants-soilingly terrifying. That’s why today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.240
we’re running down our big list of twenty-eight&nbsp;
soul-shattering phobias, and giving you the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:04.860
perfect anomaly for each one. It’s gonna get scary&nbsp;
out here, so please, don’t say we didn’t warn you!

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.560
First, we’ve got Agoraphobia: The fear&nbsp;
of open spaces. People with this phobia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.300
often avoid leaving the home, fearing that&nbsp;
they’ll have a panic attack in a wide open,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:21.600
unfamiliar space. This is precisely why anyone&nbsp;
suffering from Agoraphobia would hate to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:29.220
a run-in with SCP-093, the Red Sea Object. When&nbsp;
placed against a mirror, this unassuming little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:35.640
talisman can transport you to a nightmarish world&nbsp;
of wide, desolate deserts populated by craggy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.260
faceless giants out for your blood. With&nbsp;
nowhere safe to seclude yourself away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.780
SCP-093’s nightmarish dimension would&nbsp;
be an Agoraphobe’s living nightmare.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:51.840
Then there’s Acrophobia: The fear of&nbsp;
heights. This is an incredibly common one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.920
and if being high up enough has ever&nbsp;
induced vertigo and made your legs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.180
turn to jello beneath you, then&nbsp;
you can probably relate. But hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:08.640
simply don’t go anywhere high up, right? Nice&nbsp;
and easy. Except SCP-3007, a deadly infohazard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.640
has the terrifying ability to bring those&nbsp;
heights to you. If you’re infected by SCP-3007,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.340
you’ll have ultra-immersive hallucinations of&nbsp;
yourself teetering on the huge and impossibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:27.840
high-up walkways of a city full of silver spires.&nbsp;
And if this makes you dizzy, remember, it’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:34.380
just a dream. If you fall from a great height&nbsp;
in your hallucination, you’ll die in real life.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.340
But maybe you’d take being at the top&nbsp;
of the tower over having to deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:45.240
anything that has eight legs. That is, if you&nbsp;
have Arachnophobia: The fear of spiders. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.640
one is self-explanatory, some people are&nbsp;
just debilitatingly terrified of spiders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:56.940
and they likely think about it a lot. You might&nbsp;
even say they have Intrusive Arachnid Thoughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.340
like SCP-632, an anomaly that’s&nbsp;
likely to scare an arachnophobe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.920
to death - Literally. If you see a tiny pink&nbsp;
spider with a strange pattern on its back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:15.180
it may already be over for you, as the horrors of&nbsp;
SCP-632 flood your mind with thoughts of spiders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:21.480
as your brain matter literally transforms into&nbsp;
a vast, skittering colony of the little beasts.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.760
Maybe that last anomaly has you wanting&nbsp;
to just get up and fly away. Or maybe you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.380
suffer from Pteromerhanophobia:&nbsp;
The fear of flying. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.820
it’s nothing to be ashamed of. Unless you’re&nbsp;
enough of a baller to have a private jet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:40.680
you probably agree with everyone else&nbsp;
that flying absolutely sucks. Especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:48.000
if the flight you’re taking is SCP-787. This&nbsp;
cursed plane is filled with 515 human corpses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.340
perfectly illustrating what you fear will&nbsp;
happen to you on that plane. But it’s also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.960
the site of a wide variety of terrifying&nbsp;
anomalous happenings, from violent sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:03.660
to nightmarish figures roaming the cabin. And&nbsp;
who thought flying could possibly get any worse?

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:08.820
Next, we’re going to box you in a little, which&nbsp;
will absolutely terrify you if you suffer from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:15.240
Claustrophobia: The fear of enclosed spaces. If&nbsp;
people with claustrophobia are confined or locked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:20.880
up, they’re likely to experience a full-blown&nbsp;
panic attack. That’s why they’d utterly despise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:28.260
SCP-1562, also known as the Carnivorous&nbsp;
Slide. This seemingly ordinary tube slide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:32.400
will cause its victims to be teleported&nbsp;
to a mysterious place in total darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.880
so cramped that they can barely move, lodged&nbsp;
into place by mysterious items in the tight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:44.280
tunnel around them. And if that wasn’t scary&nbsp;
enough, you’re not alone in this terrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:49.140
claustrophobic place either. You don’t&nbsp;
want to know what happens after that.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.220
But maybe it’s not the confinement&nbsp;
that scares you in that scenario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.220 --> 00:05:00.720
but the lack of light. If that’s the case, you&nbsp;
may have Nyctophobia: The fear of the dark. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:07.080
if you do suffer from Nyctophobia, then&nbsp;
you’d absolutely hate to be stuck in SCP-087,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:12.600
the Staircase. This place is filled with&nbsp;
a kind of darkness so oppressive that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:16.860
doesn’t follow the laws of physics - No&nbsp;
matter how powerful a light you bring in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:23.040
it cannot penetrate the haze. As you descend&nbsp;
deeper into the Staircase, you’ll find that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:29.340
your sense of dread will only increase, as you&nbsp;
begin to hear a child crying far below. If you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:35.340
foolish enough to keep going, you may end up face&nbsp;
to face with a certain pale, featureless face.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:41.160
Though maybe that entity didn’t have nearly&nbsp;
enough legs to scare you. Perhaps you suffer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:48.240
from Entomophobia: The fear of insects. There are&nbsp;
honestly more insectoid SCPs than we can even list&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:53.820
right now, but for the Entomophobia sufferers in&nbsp;
our audience, we think the scariest one out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.820 --> 00:06:01.980
might be SCP-743, the Chocolate Fountain. Sounds&nbsp;
delicious, right? We hope so, because if not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:08.460
you didn’t die for much - because anyone who&nbsp;
eats the chocolate from SCP-743 is doomed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:14.100
eaten by the millions of flying ant creatures&nbsp;
within. You’ll die screaming, surrounded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:19.800
horrific buzzing and feeling a million tiny&nbsp;
legs crawling all over your body. How lovely.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:24.060
Now, picture an ocean. A vast, roiling ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:30.600
whipped to and fro by nautical winds. Maybe&nbsp;
this comforts you, or maybe it terrifies you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:37.440
because you’ve got Thalassophobia: The fear of&nbsp;
the sea. This is an incredibly popular fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.780
because let’s be real, there are a lot&nbsp;
of really scary things under the sea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:48.720
Terrifying things you’ll never forget. Or&nbsp;
maybe... Things you’ll definitely forget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:56.220
like SCP-3000, Anantashesha. This astronomically&nbsp;
large eel produces amnestics which lull its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:01.680
victims into a false sense of security before&nbsp;
devouring them. And hell, if the ocean itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:07.500
is that terrifying to you, maybe being eaten by&nbsp;
a massive eel god would be a reprieve for you.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.320
Let’s get back out of the water and onto land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:16.620
where all kinds of things are slithering. If that&nbsp;
makes you nervous, you might have Ophidiophobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:23.340
The fear of snakes. And if you do, you’re&nbsp;
going to be mortally terrified of SCP-5430,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:29.640
an Eastern garter Snake that has even greater&nbsp;
locomotive abilities than the average snake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:36.420
because it has 48 legs, connected by thaumaturgic&nbsp;
means. It’s essentially the snake equivalent of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:41.760
centipede. We don’t even have Ophidiophobia,&nbsp;
and that’s a pretty terrifying thought to us!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:48.780
But maybe we need to think a little bigger. Or&nbsp;
maybe, a lot bigger. If that sentiment makes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:55.320
feel a little nervous, though, you may suffer from&nbsp;
Megalophobia: The fear of large things. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.320 --> 00:08:03.300
many large and terrifying SCPs in this world, but&nbsp;
few are quite as dizzyingly massive as SCP-2317-K,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:08.760
also known as the Devourer of Worlds.&nbsp;
Just how big is this very hungry boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:13.020
locked away behind the door to another&nbsp;
world? According to our best estimates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:19.500
it’s a little over 200 kilometers tall,&nbsp;
roughly equivalent to 451 Empire State&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:24.060
Buildings stacked on top of each other.&nbsp;
Jeez, that makes us feel a little dizzy.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.440
Let’s stop thinking about that, and instead&nbsp;
consider the most frightening thing of all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:36.480
Spooky, scary skeletons. Skelephobia: The fear&nbsp;
of skeletons. And for those afraid of skeletons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:43.380
SCP-3114 would be an elementally terrifying&nbsp;
entity to encounter. This living skeleton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:48.960
actually hates being a skeleton, so much so that&nbsp;
if it encounters a human being who does have skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:54.720
it tears the skin off in a jealous rage&nbsp;
and wears it like a costume. So if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:09:00.000
do have Skelephobia, you’d be lucky to&nbsp;
encounter SCP-3114 when it’s wearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.500
a tasteful human skin outfit. Then I’m&nbsp;
sure it wouldn’t be terrifying at all.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:11.580
Okay, okay, it’s no secret that we sometimes like&nbsp;
to be funny here on SCP Explained. Much like Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:17.760
Bright, we use humor as a coping mechanism.&nbsp;
We’re happy to be a little clownish now and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:24.540
then. That wouldn’t be so chill for people who&nbsp;
suffer from Coulrophobia: The fear of clowns.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:30.840
And for those terrified of clowns, we know one&nbsp;
show you definitely shouldn’t watch: SCP-993,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:37.080
Bobble the Clown. This jolly cartoon nightmare is&nbsp;
a clown that loves to teach kids the tools of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:43.020
trade, like breaking and entering, murder,&nbsp;
cannibalism, and arson, just to name a few.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:47.820
If you’re afraid of clowns and you encountered&nbsp;
this show as a kid, you’d be traumatized for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:53.220
life. Thankfully, though, if you encounter it as&nbsp;
an adult, you’ll just pass out. Small mercies, eh?

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:58.380
Now, some phobias truly can wreck your life.&nbsp;
They can make you afraid of something so common,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:04.740
so ubiquitous, it makes you wonder how you&nbsp;
can even function. One example is Heliophobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:11.220
The fear of the sun. However, we’d all be sharing&nbsp;
this phobia if SCP-001, When Day Breaks, came to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:17.220
pass. Simply being exposed to the sunlight would&nbsp;
cause you to melt into a deranged blob. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:22.980
if this ever happened, people suffering from&nbsp;
Heliophobia may actually be the most likely to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:27.600
survive - Because they’ve already spent their&nbsp;
life building strategies to help them avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:33.840
the piercing gaze of the sun. So maybe keep&nbsp;
a Heliophobe in your life, just to be safe.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:39.000
Some phobias are, thankfully, a&nbsp;
lot easier for you to avoid. Take,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:44.220
for example, Coasterphobia: The fear of&nbsp;
rollercoasters. If you have this problem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:50.280
just don’t go on a rollercoaster, but&nbsp;
especially not SCP-2183, also known,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:57.240
ominously, as “The Ride Never Ends.” If you end up&nbsp;
on this ride, you’ll be hurtling through the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:02.580
screaming in terror, forever. Not fun&nbsp;
for anyone, least of all Coasterphobes.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.520
But maybe rollercoasters don’t make you&nbsp;
nervous. Maybe being watched makes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:14.160
nervous. Maybe the idea that there could be a&nbsp;
pair of mysterious eyes boring into you right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:20.940
now makes your skin crawl. If this is true,&nbsp;
you may have Scoptophobia: The fear of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:27.060
stared at. And if you have Scoptophobia, and&nbsp;
you’re not a furry who’s down ludicrously bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:34.980
then you’d be terrified after downloading the MalO&nbsp;
app, also known as SCP-1471. If you download the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:40.080
app, you’ll be stalked by the skull-faced MalO,&nbsp;
which will stare at you from all your favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:45.900
places. That’ll get your heart rate up, one&nbsp;
way or another. I’ll say no more on that.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:52.500
Hey, is it getting hot in here? Can you smell&nbsp;
smoke? Can you hear that strange cracking noise? I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:58.500
certainly hope you don’t have Pyrophobia: The fear&nbsp;
of fire. Fearing fire is honestly pretty natural,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:04.380
given it can burn you to death, especially if&nbsp;
you’re a liar who’s trapped inside SCP-2128,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:10.380
a terrifying device known as The Liars Cradle.&nbsp;
If ever you’re locked inside its deadly furnace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:15.120
you better choose your words carefully,&nbsp;
or the Cradle will detect your mistruth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:20.460
and incinerate you. And wouldn’t it suck&nbsp;
to be terrified and agonized as you die?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:27.120
But perhaps you don’t fear fire; you just fear&nbsp;
ladies that are smoking hot. This means you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:33.900
Caligynephobia: The fear of beautiful women. Yes,&nbsp;
it is real. And if you suffer from this phobia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:40.560
then you’d be terrified of SCP-056, also&nbsp;
known as A Beautiful Person. The ideal form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:45.840
of this conceited entity is famous actor Scarlet&nbsp;
Johansson, so if you’re afraid of beautiful women,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:50.460
then this entity will horrify you to&nbsp;
your core. They’re just a real jerk, too.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:56.340
What if the early 2010s were just an absolute&nbsp;
nightmare for you, because there were zombies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:03.060
everywhere. Movies, TV shows, Halloween costumes,&nbsp;
zombie walks, and more merchandise than you shake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:09.660
Negan’s baseball bat, Lucille, at. This probably&nbsp;
means you have Kinemortophobia: The fear of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:17.100
zombies. And if that is the case, stay the hell&nbsp;
away from victims of SCP-008. This lethal and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:22.740
contagious pathogen creates mindless and extremely&nbsp;
aggressive zombies whose only purpose is to spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:28.560
their disease to others, adding additional members&nbsp;
to their teeming, mindless horde. So if that’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:34.260
your thing, either keep your distance, or make&nbsp;
sure you have some SCP-500 pills close to hand.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:41.460
Next, we have another ubiquitous nightmare -&nbsp;
Hydrophobia: The fear of water. It’s everywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:47.340
and you literally need it to survive, so it’s&nbsp;
a bummer to be petrified by it. Though at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:54.000
with SCP-1128, the Aquatic Horror, you’ll have a&nbsp;
very good reason to be afraid of water. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:58.620
if you see a picture, or get a comprehensive&nbsp;
description of this massive underwater monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:04.560
no body of water is safe. From bathtubs&nbsp;
to cups to swimming pools to puddles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:08.520
the horror will stalk you&nbsp;
relentlessly, and eat you alive.

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:15.420
And now, from big horrors, to tiny one.&nbsp;
Microphobia: The fear of small things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:20.760
There’s a joke I’d like to make here, but then&nbsp;
we wouldn’t make any money on this video. Anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:27.060
for anyone paranoid about puny perils, I&nbsp;
bet it’s a nightmare to encounter SCP-165,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:32.340
the creeping, hungry sands of Tule. Because&nbsp;
while it may look like a pile of sand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:38.280
it’s actually a giant pile of almost&nbsp;
microscopic, flesh-eating mites. Sleep tight!

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:43.260
Oh, was that a thunder crack I just heard?&nbsp;
I hope nobody here suffers from Astraphobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:47.520
The fear of storms. Though I think we’d&nbsp;
all be afraid of storms if we had a run-in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:53.640
with SCP-3280, After The Storm. This is an&nbsp;
extremely dangerous blob of living water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:58.320
which is able to incorporate even more&nbsp;
water into its mass. Its favorite hobby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:02.280
is crawling into your body, stealing&nbsp;
all your water, then bursting out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:08.160
leaving you dead. And why do storms make it even&nbsp;
more dangerous? Because it gives the creature a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:14.160
heavy supply of water. And if this thing ever gets&nbsp;
into the water cycle, we’re probably all doomed.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:19.920
Let’s move from existential threats to the&nbsp;
threat of murder most fowl - and that’s fowl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:25.860
with a W. We’re talking about Alektorophobia:&nbsp;
The fear of chickens. Of course, the average&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:31.020
chicken probably couldn’t kill you - at least&nbsp;
not without considerable prep time - but killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:36.960
you is incredibly easy for the abominable&nbsp;
chicken-human hybrids known as SCP-3199,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:43.620
Humans, Refuted. These horrific creations&nbsp;
of a mad evolutionary scientist would strike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:49.380
fear into anyone, but especially someone&nbsp;
predisposed to fear chicken-like beings.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:55.500
But what if we took a fear of an animal that could&nbsp;
even kill you without any anomalous influence. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.500 --> 00:16:01.980
phobia like Cynophobia: The fear of dogs. And&nbsp;
that fear would only be made worse by a run in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:09.600
with the ominous SCP-023, also known as Black&nbsp;
Shuck. If you see this terrifying furry beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:16.080
then it means you’re going to die soon. This&nbsp;
is one dog you really can’t call a good boy.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:21.000
But hey, we’re fair and balanced here&nbsp;
at SCP Explained. That’s why we’re also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:27.000
including Elurophobia: The fear of cats. And&nbsp;
if you are afraid of cats, then you might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:33.660
one of the few people who survive a run in with&nbsp;
SCP-247, ironically dubbed “A Harmless Kitten.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:39.480
This is a lie, because this innocent-looking&nbsp;
little cat is actually a highly aggressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:45.180
fully-grown tiger that we just happen to&nbsp;
perceive as a cute, little kitten. Being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:49.920
afraid of it despite its adorable disguise&nbsp;
is probably the best way to not get mauled.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:55.560
Now, let’s go from furry to slimy.&nbsp;
That’s right, it’s Batrachophobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.560 --> 00:17:01.500
The fear of amphibians. Frogs, toads, newts.&nbsp;
If it can traverse both water and land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:06.060
you’re afraid of it. That’s why, despite&nbsp;
her good-hearted nature, you’d probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:13.020
have a heart attack if you ran into SCP-811, the&nbsp;
Swamp Woman. She’s not mean, but she is green,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:18.600
and she does excrete dangerous acidic mucus.&nbsp;
If you’re afraid of frogs, seeing this huge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:23.820
humanoid, frog-like entity would be an excellent&nbsp;
way to ruin your latest pair of tighty whities.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.900
Maybe you’re fine with frogs, though,&nbsp;
but would absolutely die on the spot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:31.860
if you were faced with a lizard. That&nbsp;
means you’ve probably got Herpetophobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:37.320
The fear of reptiles. The worst thing you&nbsp;
could possibly run into is extremely obvious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:45.180
here - SCP-682, the legendary, infamous&nbsp;
Hard to Destroy Reptile. There are some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:50.520
scary lizards out there, but none quite as&nbsp;
scary as this, because it hates all life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:55.920
including you, and probably enjoys the fact&nbsp;
that you fear it. Though for what it’s worth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:01.260
we think being utterly terrified of running&nbsp;
into this reptile is a very rational fear.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:08.460
Now, for a slightly more abstract terror:&nbsp;
Autophobia: The fear of being alone. How do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:14.700
you feel about isolation? Of being separated from&nbsp;
all your friends and family, nobody to hear you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:20.880
nobody to help you. Alone, alone, alone. If you&nbsp;
can feel your chest tightening at these words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.860
not only do you probably have Autophobia, it’d&nbsp;
be your absolute worst nightmare to be trapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:33.120
in SCP-3001, the Red Reality, where poor&nbsp;
Dr. Scranton was forced to spend the rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:38.820
eternity. You’re beyond the help of everyone&nbsp;
here, even reality itself. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:43.740
it’s a nasty, nasty place to&nbsp;
be, no matter what you fear.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:49.200
And finally, perhaps the most irrational real&nbsp;
phobia in this video - It’s Bibliophobia:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:54.960
The fear of books. Typically, books cannot&nbsp;
hurt you, unless you get a paper cut or one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.960 --> 00:19:00.600
falls on you off a shelf. There are, however,&nbsp;
notable exceptions. Perhaps the most terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:08.100
of all is SCP-140, a cursed tome known as&nbsp;
An Incomplete Chronicle, or A Chronicle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:13.620
the Daevas. Any time this book is exposed to&nbsp;
human blood, it expands and rewrites itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:20.340
bringing the nightmarish Daevite Empire closer&nbsp;
to ruling the world as it is today. In this and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:25.560
only this very specific instance, the&nbsp;
Bibliophobia is extremely justified.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:30.900
And there you have it, folks, we’re sorry for&nbsp;
giving you a mild to moderate case of the heebie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:35.760
jeebies. Which of these phobias apply to you?&nbsp;
And do you think there are any important ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:40.740
we missed? Let us know down in the comments.&nbsp;
And of course, remember to subscribe and ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:46.740
the bell to turn on notifications, or all of&nbsp;
your worst nightmares will become reality.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.740
Now go check out “What's the Scariest SCP?”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:55.140
and “25 Most Frightening SCP” for&nbsp;
more gateways to a world of terror!

